cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PinkSight, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PinkSight: multimodal DCE-MRI + clinical fusion for breast-cancer subtype characterisation and Ki-67 stratification at diagnosis"
abstract: >-
  PinkSight is a research artifact (OPSI 2026, not a clinical product) that
  characterises breast-cancer subtype and stratifies the Ki-67 proliferation
  index at diagnosis from DCE-MRI and clinical data with explainable
  cross-attention fusion. Its headline finding is an honest null: on the Duke
  cohort a clinical-only baseline carries the subtype signal and every imaging
  and fusion rung sits below it, with the fusion-versus-clinical margin not
  demonstrated at the available sample size. Every number is a within-cohort
  result on its own patient-disjoint cohort.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Team TestEin"
version: "0.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-19"
license: Apache-2.0
